shipPrompt:
Ship Projects4Me issue #{issue} ({project}, repo {repo}). A previous session implemented it on branch claude-issue-{issue} and left this handoff note:

{handoff}

Restart the timer with dev-tools/ai/ai timer {issue}, check the branch (in {repo}: git status, git diff --stat origin/dev...claude-issue-{issue}), then run /ship-issue {issue}, shipping with `dev-tools/ai/ai ship {repo} {issue} ship.json --defer-handoff` so the issue stays in_progress with you. The design review is one advisory round, not a gate: after the full suite, run `dev-tools/ai/ai design-review {repo}` once on the final tree, fix the clear findings (then re-run only the suite), and list any you leave or disagree with in the PR description for the reviewer. Never run the design review again on the same branch to get it clean; ai ship records the line only when it was. In an auto-merge milestone Agent Agamemnon merges on its merge gate (CI, the recorded test run, people), whatever the design review said. Don't run `ai handoff` yourself: end with outcome pr_opened and the PR number in `pr`, and Talos hands the issue to its merger or to {reviewer}. Read only the files the suite or the design review points at.
